(5598325, 808919, 69668, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Bear_Music:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m really sorry to hear about the time/date fiasco. I had one of those on my highest-scoring image (at that time), just after I had bought the 20D. The store had set the time/date and it was exactly 12 hours off. As it happened, I shot the winning picture at dawn on Monday, so naturally the stamp showed it to be at sunset on Sunday, before the challenge was announced :-(<br/> <br/>At least you have the Posthumous for this one (he doesn''t care about the date stamp), and you didn''t lose a ribbon, so I guess that helps?<br/> <br/>Still a wonderful shot! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Bear....I appreciate the kind words.</td>', 'Originally posted by Bear_Music: I''m really sorry to hear about the time/date fiasco. I had one of those on my highest-scoring image (at that time), just after I had bought the 20D. The store had set the time/date and it was exactly 12 hours off. As it happened, I shot the winning picture at dawn on Monday, so naturally the stamp showed it to be at sunset on Sunday, before the challenge was announced :-( At least you have the Posthumous for this one (he doesn''t care about the date stamp), and you didn''t lose a ribbon, so I guess that helps? Still a wonderful shot!   Thanks Bear....I appreciate the kind words.', '2009-08-04 12:20:41.000000', NULL, 0),
